/E (Population, population density and CO2 emissions also have long right tails. Unemployment and infant mortality are right-skewed as well, while life expectancy and school enrollment tend to cluster toward the higher end of their observed ranges. These patterns point to substantial differences in country size and development conditions; they also explain why comparisons based only on means can be misleading.)
