/Title (The main substantive finding is that homicide rates differ sharply across countries and regions. In the cleaned analysis, the median homicide rate is 2.5 while the mean is 6.5, showing that a relatively small number of countries with high rates pull the average upward. Central America, the Caribbean and Southern Africa have the highest regional median rates in the notebook's analysis. Several health, education and development indicators move together, but no single indicator explains homicide rates on its own.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
