/Title (The cleaned notebook reports 192 countries. Homicide rates have a mean of 6.5 and a median of 2.5. The mean being substantially higher than the median is a sign of a right-skewed distribution: most countries have comparatively low rates, while a smaller group has much higher rates.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 551 0 R
/Next 577 0 R
>>
endobj
570 0 obj
<<
/Title (The notebook also notes that 26 countries share a homicide rate of exactly 2.5. Because 2.5 is the dataset median, this concentration is consistent with median imputation. That is plausible, but the value pattern alone does not prove how each value was created. If these values were imputed, they should not be interpreted as measured country-specific rates.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 551 0 R
/Prev 577 0 R
>>
endobj
